WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
-Why are you
the district attorney?

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:06.172
Or are you just the illusion
of the district attorney?

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.308
-'Cause I'm the hero
of that story.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.409
And as long as people
still believe in justice

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:14.414
and there's a system in place
that looks like it works,

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:18.417
I'm doing what the city
pays me to do.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:21.320
-[ Exhales sharply ]

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.157
Who the [bleep]
wants to be any part of that?

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.592
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.460
That was a clip
from "Perry Mason,"

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.462
starring this guy, Matthew Rhys.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.899
Now, I do have
"Perry Mason" questions,

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.099
but we mentioned your boat,
Rarebit.

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.368
And this is -- you are --

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.270
Again, this speaks
to the kind of guest you are.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.872
You have brought two foods.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:43.276
Because rarebit
I know to be a food, and I am --

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.877
But yet I don't know what it is.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.646
-Right. So, sorry.
I should have qualified.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.715
There is a traditional
Welsh dish called Welsh rarebit,

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:52.885
which is basically
cheese on toast.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.655
Which speaks
to the kind of culinary,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.324
you know, prowess that I have.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.792
That's about
the sum total of it.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.460
-And you make --
you do make this

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.828
for your guests on your boat.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.664
-So I came up
with this ingenious idea

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.200
that what I should do
when I'm aboard

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.402
is prepare them
small Welsh rarebits,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.170
which is just
toasted bread, cheese.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.106
I have --
There is no oven or grill

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.575
or broiler, anything,
so I use a blowtorch on --

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.709
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.744
On a wooden boat.
-It's a wooden boat, yeah.

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.146
I wanted to clarify that.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.714
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.550
-So they must be very excited
when they see an actor,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.287
not a sailor or a captain.
-No, no.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.856
Like, I tell people,
"Look, I've played a sailor.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.423
I've played a chef.
It's like...

00:01:31.423 --> 00:01:33.793
[ Light laughter ]
How badly can this go?

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.061
I just think
it adds to the drama.

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:37.497
I think it adds
to the drama of it all.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.732
-Give us a sense
of what they're seeing.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.568
-So what I do --
So, in fairness,

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.270
your show, I don't think,
trusted me

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.872
with the kind of blowtorch
that I use.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.174
-Okay.
-Mine's bigger, obviously.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.042
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.411
So I --
I have to make it quickly.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:53.679
Therefore,
I use a large blowtorch.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.381
And I think
it adds to the drama.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.983
'Cause you see them going,
"Will we make it home alive?"

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.085
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.486
-It's like, even I say,
"I don't know.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:01.754
Let's see how it goes.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.990
Do you like
cheese and toasted bread?"

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.157
So all I --
-It is a funny thing

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:06.492
to risk your life for.
-It is.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.661
But, basically,
this is the sped-up version

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.962
we've done for you.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:12.232
-So all I'm doing,
although this isn't --

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.433
The boat version -- right? --
'cause it's always rockin',

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.402
so choppy, it's like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.072
-Right. Yeah, yeah,
I wouldn't want to see that.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.206
-You're kind of doing that.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.574
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.077
-And, also, it should be noted,
this is you making it

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:27.046
on the boat,
and that's a real beard

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.781
you had for a while there.
-It's a fake beard.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.516
I put on the wig
and the beard 'cause I'm like,

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:31.951
"Arr!
Welcome to the boat!"

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.153
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.687
And they're like,
"We can see the glue.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.188
It doesn't work."

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:38.090
So, basically, that's all I do.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.492
And then I offer up
showbiz tales

00:02:40.492 --> 00:02:43.595
and all sorts and try
and wake them up for the end.

00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:44.897
-You said --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.033
You said the boat
is from the '30s.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.336
On "Perry Mason,"
you were on a '30s motorcycle.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.171
-I was.
-And this is practical.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.740
You're riding this motorcycle.
-It is practical.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.410
However, on the first day,
they say, "Come do your trial --

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.112
you know, your training
on the Harley-Davidson."

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:03.616
And then the guy who -- "Right,
this is how you start it.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.651
You turn this, you pull that,
you push this.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:06.852
Wait for that to kick in.

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:09.455
Now push that, pull that again,
and you're off."

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.024
And I was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.059
And the producer
saw the wild-eyed panic

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.527
in my eyes and went, "Okay.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:18.164
We need a montage to do just
the starting of the motorbike."

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.632
Told the action guy vehicle,

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.768
"Turn it into
an electric bike in a week."

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.904
-Yeah.
-So it kind of split --

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.674
A number of people who,
when we were shooting outside,

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.907
would come out and say,
"Oh, my God.

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:31.444
Is this a 1933 Harley?"
They're like, "It is."

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.745
They're like,
"Why can't we hear it?"

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.048
And I'd say, [weakly]
"It's an electric bike now."

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.348
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:39.118
And it would split.
50% of these predominantly men

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.620
of a certain age would go,
"That's incredible.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.887
You've turned it
into an electric bike,"

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:43.890
and 50% would say,
"That's disgusting,

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.391
what you've done to that hog."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.859
-I would say, like, yeah.
-I get it.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.094
-This, though, there's
no shortcut with horses.

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:51.730
-There was no shortcuts.
-Now, this is you on a horse.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.967
-That's me on a horse.
-That's you on a horse.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:57.870
-There's no CGI.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.340
-Can I ask why --
-No saddle in that picture.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.542
-Look at that!
No saddle.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.809
-Yeah, yeah.
-It's interesting

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.077
'cause saddles --
you would think you'd need

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.411
a saddle for safety.

00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:09.115
You're doing no saddle,
but you are wearing a mask.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.517
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.719
-The horse was an anti-vaxxer.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.688
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.956
Or had COVID.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.257
I couldn't understand
what he was trying to say.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.326
-Right, right, right.
It's very hard.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.994
It's hard.
-It's hard.

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.996
It's hard for them.
-Now, did you have any

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.365
previous experience on a horse,
because this looks terrifying.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.902
-I actually did, and I did that
slightly foolish thing.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.336
The writers very kindly said,

00:04:31.336 --> 00:04:32.905
"Is there anything
you want to do in a scene?"

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.774
And I was like,
"I love riding horses."

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.742
But they put me on a scene
where the horse rears.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.945
I was like,
"I don't like horses that rear."

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.846
I like riding -- riding them.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.881
-But it was a --
I loved it.

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:44.516
I bonded with the horse.
-Well, there you go.

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.385
And you guys will probably
work together again.

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:49.154
-I hope so.
-Now, you've talked in the past,

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:50.556
again, one of
my all-time favorite shows

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.124
where you met your partner,
Keri.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.160
-Yeah.
-And by the way, you guys,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.995
congratulations.
"Cocaine Bear."

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.597
Unbelievable.
-Amazing. Yeah.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:00.433
Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.267
-The two of you
collaborating again.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.370
And also with Margo Martindale
from "The Americans."

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.806
-It was an "Americans" reunion.
We loved it.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.774
But congratulations,
Elizabeth Banks,

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:10.809
who pulled that
incredible movie off.

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:12.845
-It's a delight.
It's the kind of movie

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.180
that people want to go see
in theaters again,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.814
and we just need
more and more of those.

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:17.450
-I say yes.
-But "The Americans,"

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.118
you were very honest,
which I appreciated,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.719
that it was
a very complicated plot.

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.421
And, you know,
there was a lot of subterfuge

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.723
and a lot of people pretending.
And you just straight-up

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:27.193
admitted to us
you could never follow it.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:30.362
-I had the entire production
team, the entire writing staff.

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:32.031
I still was like, "I have
no idea what's going on."

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.365
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:36.569
I freely admit I'm not
the sharpest tool in the box.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.772
I'm probably the biggest tool
in the wardrobe.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.406
But I'm like,
"This is so complicated.

00:05:41.406 --> 00:05:42.875
I have no idea what's going on."
-Look, some people

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.777
can follow plots, and some
people are leek eaters.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.311
-I like to think
I'm the Everyman.

00:05:46.311 --> 00:05:49.382
I'm like, "Look, if
I understand it, we're golden."

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.250
If not --"
And everyone will be going,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.985
"We all understand it
except you."

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.321
And I'm like, "All right."

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.155
I'm thinking for the other...
half?

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:59.224
-Because "Perry Mason" --
now it's "Perry Mason."

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:03.162
It's a courtroom drama.
It's, you know, legal maneuvers.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.297
Are you the same?

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.664
-I had no idea
what was going on.

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.533
-Yeah.
-I was forever going,

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.668
"Who is he?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.437
He's like, "That's the guy
you're defending!"

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.405
I was like, "What? I thought
I was defending the other guy."

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:15.674
"That's his brother!"
I was like, "oh, my God."

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.175
This is --
My head is spinning.

00:06:17.175 --> 00:06:18.744
-You're a fantastic actor

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.546
because you come off
so sharp on camera.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.913
-That's where my acting --

00:06:21.913 --> 00:06:23.549
that's where the acting
comes in.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.850
-Yeah.
Unbelievable.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.118
[ Applause ]
-Unbelievable.

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:29.288
-Well, I really -- you know,
I know you're a busy man

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.423
and, you know, scheduling
is always an issue.

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:34.192
But, man, we should make
St. David's a tradition here.

00:06:34.192 --> 00:06:35.461
-Bring back day drinking.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.095
We'll do it on March the 1st.
-Oh, there you go.

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.031
Day drinking with a Welsh theme.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.400
Matthew Rhys!
Second season of "Perry Mason"

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.869
premieres March 6th
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:45.905
We'll be right back
with Francia Raisa.

